gopuml
==============

This project is a Go reimplementation of PlantUML (https://plantuml.com,
https://github.com/plantuml/plantuml).

Upstream origin
---------------

Source files that carry a "Provenance: plantuml-mit 1.2026.9 <path>" header
are translations of the MIT-licensed variant of PlantUML v1.2026.9, as
published on Maven Central:

    net.sourceforge.plantuml:plantuml-mit:1.2026.9:sources

    (C) Copyright 2009-2024, Arnaud Roques
    Licensed under the MIT License.

Files with a "Provenance: fdlibm 5.3 <file>" header are translations of
fdlibm, the C math library behind Java's StrictMath:

    Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved.
    Developed at SunSoft, a Sun Microsystems, Inc. business.
    Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this software is freely
    granted, provided that this notice is preserved.

Files with a "Provenance: original" header are original work of this project.

Excluded upstream components
----------------------------

The following PlantUML components are not part of the MIT variant and are not
included in this project: ditaa, jcckit, sudoku, zxing (QR codes), and the
webp decoder.

Ten of upstream's themes, among them "sunlust" (GPL-3.0-or-later), are not
bundled; see "Bundled themes" below.

Bundled assets
--------------

internal/tim/javatimezone_data.go lists the time zone display names that
java.util.TimeZone returns in OpenJDK 21 (from the JDK's CLDR and time zone
locale data), so that %date() prints the same zone names as upstream. The
CLDR data is Copyright (C) Unicode, Inc., licensed under the Unicode License
v3 (https://www.unicode.org/license.txt).

internal/klimt/svg/glyphs/dejavu.bin holds glyph outlines derived from the
DejaVu fonts, used to center circled characters as upstream does. DejaVu
fonts are (C) Bitstream, Inc. and Tavmjong Bah, with DejaVu changes in the
public domain; see internal/klimt/svg/glyphs/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt.

internal/klimt/g2d/dejavu/fonts/ holds the DejaVu fonts 2.37 (DejaVu Sans,
DejaVu Sans Mono and DejaVu Serif, each in four styles), unmodified and
compressed with gzip, which the PNG output draws text with. Copyright (c)
2003 by Bitstream, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Bitstream Vera is a trademark
of Bitstream, Inc. Copyright (c) 2006 by Tavmjong Bah. All Rights Reserved.
DejaVu changes are in public domain. The fonts are distributed under the
Bitstream Vera and Arev fonts licenses, reproduced in
internal/klimt/g2d/dejavu/fonts/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt.

Bundled themes
--------------

internal/themes/ holds 34 of the 44 theme files of PlantUML v1.2026.9 (the
themes/ folder of the plantuml-mit jar), as PlantUML distributes them, without
further changes. "!theme <name>" and "--theme <name>" load them.

aws-orange, black-knight, bluegray, cerulean, cerulean-outline,
cloudscape-design, cyborg, cyborg-outline, hacker, lightgray, materia,
materia-outline, metal, minty, sandstone, silver, sketchy, sketchy-outline,
spacelab, superhero, superhero-outline and united come from puml-themes by
Brett Schwarz (https://github.com/bschwarz/puml-themes). spacelab-white is the
spacelab theme adapted by KingPlus-lang (only its name and background color
differ). They are Copyright (c) 2020 Brett Schwarz and licensed under the MIT
License, reproduced in internal/themes/LICENSE-MIT-puml-themes.txt.

reddress-darkblue, reddress-darkgreen, reddress-darkorange, reddress-darkred,
reddress-lightblue, reddress-lightgreen, reddress-lightorange and
reddress-lightred come from RedDress-PlantUML by Drakemor
(https://github.com/Drakemor/RedDress-PlantUML), licensed under the MIT
License as its README states.

mars, toy and vibrant come from puml-themes by Future Corporation
(https://github.com/future-architect/puml-themes):

    Copyright 2020 Future Corporation. Japan

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
    you may not use these files except in compliance with the License.
    You may obtain a copy of the License at

        http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

    Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
    distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
    WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
    See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
    limitations under the License.

A copy of the License is in internal/themes/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt. The
source repository has no NOTICE file. PlantUML modified these files (it
replaced their comment header with a YAML metadata header); this project
ships them as PlantUML v1.2026.9 does.

The following upstream themes are not bundled:

- sunlust (Artem V. Ageev): its header declares the license "GPL 3+"
  (GPL-3.0-or-later), which cannot be distributed under this project's MIT
  License.
- _none_ (The-Lum), amiga, blueprint, crt-amber, crt-green, mimeograph,
  plain (Matthew Leather), mono (Denis Bondarenko and Matthew Leather) and
  carbon-gray (Bharat Rajagopalan): their files have no license line, and
  neither the upstream history of the files (the commits and pull requests
  that added them) nor upstream's LICENSES.md states a license for them, so
  their license could not be verified.

For these names, "!theme <name>" reports upstream's error for an unknown
theme ("Cannot load theme <name>"), unless a local file
puml-theme-<name>.puml is found, and %get_all_theme() does not list them.

